Description: Fast, stateless, deterministic random number generation.
    Random values are pure functions of immutable keys and sampler
    arguments, so sampling never reads or mutates '.Random.seed', and
    output is bit-identical across platforms and thread counts. The default
    engine is xoshiro256++ (Blackman and Vigna, 2021)
    <doi:10.1145/3460772>, reseeded from the Philox counter-based generator
    of the 'Random123' library (Salmon, Moraes, Dror and Shaw, 2011)
    <doi:10.1145/2063384.2063405>; Philox and Threefry are also available
    directly. Normal deviates use the ziggurat method (Marsaglia and Tsang,
    2000) <doi:10.18637/jss.v005.i08>. Independent substreams are requested
    as key vectors with rng_key(seed, n) or derived explicitly with
    rng_fold().
